  "notes": "ろ{過|か} means to pass a liquid or gas through a filter to remove impurities.\n\nWRITING:\nThe full kanji form is {濾|ろ}{過|か}, but since {濾|ろ} is not in the {常用|じょうよう}{漢字|かんじ} list, it is normally written in mixed form as ろ{過|か}.\n\nCOMMON COLLOCATIONS:\n- ろ{過|か}する: to filter\n- ろ{過|か}{装置|そうち}: filtration device/equipment\n- ろ{過|か}{器|き}: filter (the device itself)\n- ろ{過|か}{水|すい}: filtered water\n\nUSAGE:\nUsed in scientific, industrial, and everyday contexts. Coffee brewing, water purification, and laboratory work all use ろ{過|か}. The noun can be used with する to form the verb \"to filter.\"",
